detailed_feedback: "The candidate shows promise with their computer science education and general software engineering experience. Their Python knowledge, while present, appears focused on machine learning rather than web development. The GitHub profile demonstrates coding ability and project completion, but the projects don't align closely with backend web development requirements.\n\nThe lack of experience with FastAPI, async Python, and database technologies presents a significant learning curve for this role. While the candidate could potentially learn these technologies, they would require substantial training and ramp-up time to become productive in the position.\n\nTheir experience at JetBrains and Deutsche Börse suggests they can work in professional development environments, but the technical stack mismatch means they would essentially be starting from scratch with many of the core technologies used in this role."
hiring_manager_notes: "Consider that while the candidate shows strong general software engineering capabilities, they would need significant training in our tech stack. Their background suggests they can learn quickly, but expect 3-6 months before full productivity.\n\nIf you're open to training someone with good fundamentals but no direct experience, they could be worth considering. However, if you need someone who can hit the ground running with FastAPI and async Python, this candidate may not be the best fit.\n\nRecommendation: Consider for junior role if willing to invest in training, but may want to continue searching if seeking an experienced backend developer."